            <!-- Douro River Cruise -->
            <p>
              <a href="https://www.viator.com/en-AU/tours/Porto/Private-Cruise-on-the-Douro-River-with-Tapas-and-Port-Wine/d26879-356132P3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <strong>Douro River Cruise</strong>
              </a>
              - Short, scenic boat cruises within Porto that focus on the city rather than the upriver wine valley. 
              These relaxed trips highlight the Ribeira waterfront, wine cellars of Vila Nova de Gaia, historic landmarks along the riverbanks, and Porto’s iconic bridges.
              There are many operators offering similar routes. 
              My wife and I opted for a private boat, which meant a modern motorboat instead of a traditional vessel, but also a private guide and a charcuterie board prepared by our hosts. 
              The cruise lasted about an hour and was relaxed and enjoyable. 
              Since it takes place on the river, the water is calm and seasickness isn’t a concern. 
              Just be mindful of the pickup location, as some docks are farther from the main areas than others.
            </p>
