          <section class="two-column section-wide">
            <div class="section">
              <h2>Food &amp; Drink</h2>
              <p>
                Meals in Porto are rich in fresh, local ingredients, focusing on the "Atlantic Diet" with abundant seafood, vegetables, fruits, and whole grains, alongside staples like pork, legumes, rice, and potatoes. 
                Try a francesinha, ideally somewhere locals actually eat rather than the main riverfront strip. 
                The waterfront is scenic but comes with predictable markups.
                Port wine is exceptional in Porto, and much of it never leaves Europe.
                Serious wine enthusiasts are missing out if they skip Porto and the Douro Valley.
              </p>

